Mobile data over the mainline Linux IPA driver (Qualcomm SoCs such as the
Pro1X's SM6115, IPA v4.2): oFono 2.18's qrtrsoc modem only knew the premux
interfaces of Android kernels (rmnet_data*, made and set up by others), and
its rmnet module deletes every rmnet link it finds when it starts, those
included. With the mainline driver there is only rmnet_ipa0, and the data
port needs what ModemManager's qcom-soc support does (src/mm-port-qmi.c,
ModemManager 1.24.2):

- udevng: a rmnet_ipa device of the mainline driver (sysfs
  device/modem/rx_endpoint_id, drivers/net/ipa/ipa_sysfs.c) makes a qrtrqmi
  modem without premux interfaces (path still /qrtrsoc_N);
- qrtrqmi: for such an embedded modem, DPM "Open Port" (service 0x2f,
  message 0x0020, TLV 0x11 as libqmi 1.38's qmi-service-dpm.json) with the
  IPA's modem endpoints from sysfs, WDA "Set Data Format" on the embedded
  port (endpoint type 4, interface 1): raw IP with QMAPv5, else QMAPv4,
  else QMAP, each read back; then four rmnet links with the checksum
  offload of sysfs device/feature/{rx,tx}_offload ("MAPv4" below IPA v4.5);
  any failure or no answer within 20 s only leaves the modem without data
  contexts (calls and SMS stay); OFONO_IPA_WDA, OFONO_IPA_DPM and
  OFONO_IPA_RMNET_FLAGS in ofonod's environment change these steps for tests
  on a device;
- rmnet: rmnet_get_interfaces_flags(), the links' data format as a
  parameter (rmnet_get_interfaces keeps QMAPv5's).

For pro1x-maemo-leste (github smatkovi/pro1x-maemo-leste,
scripts/49-mobile-data.sh), against Maemo Leste's ofono 1:2.18.0-1+4m7.1.

